  "pages": {
    "format": {
      "url": "https://www.lorekit.io/blog/open-agent-memory-format",
      "label": "lorekit.io",
      "name": "Agent memory needs its OpenTelemetry moment",
      "highlights": [
        {
          "id": "shape",
          "text": "Every agent tool stores memory in its own shape",
          "zh": "每种工具各自存记忆。"
        },
        {
          "id": "none",
          "text": "None of them can read the others.",
          "zh": "谁也读不了谁的。"
        },
        {
          "id": "otel",
          "text": "OpenTelemetry gave everyone one data model to share",
          "zh": "OpenTelemetry 给了大家同一套数据模型"
        },
        {
          "id": "four",
          "text": "That's four different shapes, and none of them can read the others.",
          "zh": "四种形状，谁也读不了谁的。"
        },
        {
          "id": "agree",
          "text": "The problem isn't a missing tool. It's a missing agreement",
          "zh": "缺的不是工具，是一份约定"
        },
        {
          "id": "pitch",
          "text": "This isn't a pitch that LoreKit has solved memory.",
          "zh": "这不是在说 LoreKit 已经解决了记忆。"
        },
        {
          "id": "y2019",
          "text": "Before 2019, every observability vendor shipped its own agent",
          "zh": "2019 年前，各家都发自己的采集器"
        },
        {
          "id": "merge",
          "text": "In 2019 they merged into OpenTelemetry.",
          "zh": "2019 年它们合并成了 OpenTelemetry。"
        },
        {
          "id": "once",
          "text": "Users instrument once.",
          "zh": "用户只埋点一次。"
        },
        {
          "id": "where",
          "text": "Agent memory is where observability was before 2019.",
          "zh": "记忆所处的阶段，像 2019 年前的可观测性。"
        },
        {
          "id": "days",
          "text": "Deleted after 28 days unused",
          "zh": "28 天不用就删掉"
        },
        {
          "id": "path",
          "text": "a plain file at a known path can become a standard",
          "zh": "已知路径上的普通文件，可以变成标准"
        },
        {
          "id": "export",
          "text": "These mostly solve export",
          "zh": "这些方案大多在解决导出"
        },
        {
          "id": "live",
          "text": "how do they read and write the same place",
          "zh": "它们怎样读写同一个地方"
        },
        {
          "id": "both",
          "text": "A complete spec needs both.",
          "zh": "一份完整规格两样都要。"
        },
        {
          "id": "who",
          "text": "A spec doesn't need to pick one. It needs to record which, so a reader knows how much to trust what it reads.",
          "zh": "规格不必选边，但要记下是谁写的。"
        },
        {
          "id": "call",
          "text": "MCP standardises the call, not the record.",
          "zh": "MCP 标准化的是调用，不是记录。"
        },
        {
          "id": "span",
          "text": "A span is written once and never changes.",
          "zh": "一条 span 写下之后就不再改。"
        },
        {
          "id": "poison",
          "text": "No format makes poisoning impossible.",
          "zh": "没有哪种格式能让投毒变得不可能。"
        },
        {
          "id": "xkcd",
          "text": "agreement came when existing projects merged, not when someone added another one.",
          "zh": "约定来自合并，不是再加一个新标准。"
        },
        {
          "id": "forkw",
          "text": "There's one real fork: who writes the memory.",
          "zh": "真正的分叉是谁来写。"
        }
      ],
      "figures": [
